  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 205 AM CDT Mon May 11 2026\n\nToday through Sunday night:\n\nA frontal boundary extends across the Delta tonight, with a few \nshowers/storms mainly east of I-55. The front will slowly drop \nsoutheast across the area through the day, with a scattered \nshowers/storms possible early this afternoon, but drier air will \nbuild in behind the front, with the showers shifting south of the\narea by this evening. Surface high pressure will build over the \narea tonight into Tuesday. A nice day is on tap for Tuesday with \nhighs in the low 80s under mostly sunny skies. Little will change \non Wednesday, but a dry cold front will move across the area on \nThursday. The dry conditions will continue into the weekend, but \nthe global models suggest and increase in moisture and chances for\nshowers/storms on Sunday./15/",
